    "title": "Fairhope Police called to assist in removing large alligator - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Hanich ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: From the WKRG.com Archives — Family finds alligator in their backyard pool\nFAIRHOPE, Ala. (WKRG) — The Fairhope Police Department said they carefully removed a large alligator near downtown Fairhope.\nAccording to an FPD Facebook post , officers were called Tuesday, Aug. 11, about an eight-foot-long gator approaching downtown Fairhope. Officers didn’t say which neighborhood the gator was first seen.\nJerry Carl wins GOP nomination in Alabama’s District 1 Special Congressional race The post said officers assisted a state wildlife expert in removing the gator from the road.\nOfficials said the large reptile was taken to a habitat more suited for its species.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "According to an FPD Facebook post , officers were called Tuesday, Aug. 11, about an eight-foot-long gator approaching downtown Fairhope. Jerry Carl wins GOP nomination in Alabama’s District 1 Special Congressional race The post said officers assisted a state wildlife expert in removing the gator from the road. Officials said the large reptile was taken to a habitat more suited for its species. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
